Z||000000||bHooper||02-09-2001||12:46 PM||||page 21, the "Your Turn" section... allow me to paraphrase (did i spell that right, if not im sorry) a letter by <B>Matthew Fillcetti</B> (PFF Member, perhaps?) of Racine Wisconsin<P><B>IF THE 914, THEN...</B><BR>As a owner of a '85 Pontiac Fiero SE, 6 cyl, I was somwhat surprised that no credit was given to my car on your "Mid-Engine Magic Timeline" (December'00).  I am certainly aware that the car is far from perfect, and not in the class of Ferrari's, and Porsches (bHooper note:<B>rear engined car</B>), but it remaines the only mid-engined car ever produced by an american company... even pacing the Indy 500.<P>You may not see the Fiero as significant, but it deserves better mention than, "and, yes, even Pontiac."  Many would say that the Fiero is no less significant that tht Porsche 914.  Come on and give this American car it's place in the timeline.<P>(words have been editied to protect the unknown)<P>the second response to this topic was a fellow who was upset that the Pantera was left out... <B> at least we're keeping some good company!</B><P>hoop||||reg||1
